  concept: "Authored objective: Verify the receiver pull-up.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from solved LED current, receiver voltage, and wire topology. voltage
    \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching principle: An LED has a
    defined anode and cathode; correct polarity and suitable current control matter
    for normal forward operation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
